CKS-Notes

The kubeconfig file is generally located in the home directory under .kube folder

It has the below structure.

apiVersion: v1
clusters:
 - list of clusters [Each cluster has name, server URL and CA data]
contexts:
 - list of contexts[ which is a combination of cluster, user and optionally 
 namespace]
users:
 - list of users
 Each user can be authenticated via various means.
 For certificate based authentication, the mechanism is
 you will see client certificate data and client key data 
========


SAMPLE KUBECONFIG FILE 
=======
apiVersion: v1
clusters:
- cluster:
    certificate-authority-data: xxxxx
    server: https://192.168.100.21:6443
  name: gianna@infra-prod
contexts:
- context:
    cluster: gianna@infra-prod
    user: gianna@infra-prod
  name: gianna@infra-prod
kind: Config
preferences: {}
users:
- name: gianna@infra-prod
  user:
    client-certificate-data: xxxxx
    client-key-data: xxxxxx=
